    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #316\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-211-implementation-audit-fixes-01-23-norma-thr_w8rtk87tic`.\n\n## Summary\n\nPushed the fix for the code-review findings on PR #316:\n\n- **High-severity finding fixed**: `deleteRelationWithClient` no longer calls `assertRelationEndpointsValid`. That check was correct for create/update, but it broke real cleanup callers (`inboxTypesStore`'s `deleteInboxTypeWithClient`, and the Gmail/Graph/IMAP reconcilers) that delete an edge after one of its endpoints was already soft-deleted — the normalized `(relationDefinitionId, itemA, itemB)` lookup is safe regardless of endpoint state, so delete stays truly idempotent.\n- **Medium-severity finding fixed**: added an integration test covering delete after the target endpoint is soft-deleted, confirming it still resolves to `undefined`.\n\nVerified with the full check suite: backend build (clean), unit tests (83/83), integration tests (391/391, real Postgres), e2e tests (5/5), migration numbering check, dependency boundaries check, and web build + tests (81/81) — all green.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
