    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #316\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-211-implementation-audit-fixes-01-23-norma-thr_w8rtk87tic`.\n\n## Summary\n\nPushed the fix for the remaining code-review findings on PR #316:\n\n- **High-severity finding fixed**: `copyRelationEdges` in `advanceTaskRecurrence.ts` now checks the liveness of an edge's counterpart item before calling `createRelationWithClient`, and skips (rather than propagates) an edge whose linked item was soft-deleted since the edge was created. Previously the new endpoint validation could abort the entire recurrence-advance transaction over one stale relation link — now the advance succeeds and simply drops that edge.\n- **Medium-severity finding fixed**: added an integration test in `tenDatabases.test.ts` reproducing the exact regression (soft-delete a linked project, then advance the recurrence and confirm it still succeeds with the stale edge dropped), plus a test in `relations.test.ts` documenting the intentional update/delete asymmetry (update on a soft-deleted endpoint is `validation_failed`; delete stays idempotent).\n\nVerified with the full check suite: backend build (clean), unit tests (83/83), integration tests (393/393, real Postgres), e2e tests (5/5), migration numbering check, dependency boundaries check, and web build + tests (81/81) — all green.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
