    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #316\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-211-implementation-audit-fixes-01-23-norma-thr_w8rtk87tic`.\n\n## Summary\n\nPushed the fix for the remaining medium-severity finding on PR #316: `updateRelationWithClient` and `deleteRelationWithClient` share the same `loadRelationEdgeContext` → `normalizeRelationSides` pipeline as `createRelationWithClient`, but only create's inverse (B-side) path had test coverage. Added three tests to `relations.test.ts`:\n\n- Update through the inverse `property_id_b` mutates the exact edge created through `property_id_a` (same `id`, correct `itemA`/`itemB`, correct metadata).\n- Update on a missing edge through `property_id_b` returns `404 not_found` with the B-side property id and caller/target ids in the caller's own frame.\n- Delete through `property_id_b` removes the edge created through `property_id_a`.\n\nVerified with the full check suite: backend build (clean), unit tests (83/83), integration tests (396/396 on rerun — one initial run hit an unrelated transient `deadlock detected` flake inside the test harness's `resetDatabase`, in a file unrelated to this change), e2e tests (5/5), migration numbering check, dependency boundaries check, and web build + tests (81/81) — all green.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
